A||||3||Gary W||A Holiday thought....||||1||
Z||000000||Gary W||11-28-2001||10:12 PM||||Shamelessly cut & pasted from the Dilbert Newsletter by Scott Adams:<P>My Holiday Message<BR>------------------<P>I've written and rewritten this section a dozen times. My problem<BR>is that no matter how much I write, I keep condensing it down to<BR>the same thought: This holiday season, as we laugh and eat and shop<BR>and enjoy friends and family, our soldiers are in Afghanistan<BR>risking everything for us. Some of them won't come back. The rest<BR>will never be the same. <P>Every one of them volunteered. They think we're worth it.<P>Let's prove them right.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||11-28-2001||10:24 PM||||Hate to rain on anybodies parade, but that message should have included war veterans as well. Secondly, would you treat a service person different if he was drafted. I'm sure the writer had very good intentions, just didn't come through a 100% for me. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||11-29-2001||12:07 AM||||Calif Kid, are draftees different? You betcha. They were somewhere they didn't want to be, doing a job they didn't ask for. But, they did it anyway, and did it well at that.<BR>Brothers all.||||reg||14
